{number: 71}
{title: Something for Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Savior, Thy dying love Thou gavest [G7] me,
Nor should I [C] aught withhold, [F] dear Lord, from [C] Thee:
In love my [F] soul would bow, my heart ful-[C] fill its vow,
Some off'ring [G7] bring Thee now, something for [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
At [C] the blest mercy seat, pleading for [G7] me,
My feeble [C] faith looks up, [F] Jesus, to [C] Thee:
Help me the [F] cross to bear, Thy wondrous [C] love declare,
Some song to [G7] raise, or prayer, something for [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Give [C] me a faithful heart, likeness to [G7] Thee,
That each de-[C] parting day [F] henceforth may [C] see
Some work of [F] love begun, some deed of [C] kindness done,
Some wand'rer [G7] sought and won, something for [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
